+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Little River, SC a city, and what county is it in?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Little River is not a city. It is an unincorporated community in Horry County, South Carolina, at the North Carolina line, and the county runs it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is there to do in Little River, SC?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most of Little River's life is on the water: the docks and restaurants on the Mineola Avenue waterfront, and public ramps on the waterway and the Waccamaw River. On land there is golf in the neighborhoods, the trails at Vereen Memorial Historical Gardens and the Blue Crab Festival each May."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How far is Little River from Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About 36 minutes by car to Coastal Grand Mall in Myrtle Beach, without traffic. Barefoot Landing, in North Myrtle Beach, is about 18 minutes, and the airport about 41."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Little River, SC flood?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most of it does not: about 96 in 100 homes are outside FEMA's high-risk flood zone. The risk is at the water's edge, along the Intracoastal Waterway."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the property tax in Little River, SC?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A home you live in pays only the county's property tax, about $1,400 a year on a typical resold house, with no city tax on top. A second home or rental is taxed at a higher rate."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much is a boat slip in Little River?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Deeded slips at Mariner's Pointe, most about 30 to 35 feet long, sold for $10,000 to $38,000 in the past year, each on its own deed, without a condo. Bigger slips at Dock Holidays, across the line in North Myrtle Beach, sold for $65,000 to $115,000."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Little River, SC safe?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We do not rate any place as safe or unsafe. Reported crime is published by police agency, and we pull the figures for the area around any house you ask about."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which schools serve Little River, SC?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Horry County Schools assigns schools by address, in nine attendance areas, and none is named Little River. We look up the assigned schools for any house you like."}}]}</script>
